{"type":"text","timestamp":1794318950894,"sessionID":"ses_e3a41e784ffewW0a3KF7BSFPAW","part":{"id":"prt_1c5be61b7001xPOT4N2UPKvH4J","messageID":"msg_1c5be4e560011BpCSN0yQ2NHLN","sessionID":"ses_e3a41e784ffewW0a3KF7BSFPAW","type":"text","text":"<think>The lock file has flask, gunicorn, werkzeug. I'll need to add dependencies for password hashing and tokens. Let me check what's available in the pip cache. The task says \"The sandbox can install packages from the public package registries (through a read-only cache)\".\n\nI could avoid adding dependencies by using Python's stdlib `hashlib` (pbkdf2_hmac) for password hashing and `hmac`/`secrets` for tokens stored in the DB. That avoids needing new packages. That's simpler and safer given the lock file constraint. Let me do that.\n\nLet me check whether pip can install anything (network access) and whether npm works for tailwind.\n\nLet me check the npm cache availability for tailwindcss and the vite plugin.\n\nPlan:\n1. Backend: Flask app with SQLite, auth (register/login with token), todos CRUD, pagination, filtering, sorting.\n2. Frontend: React + TS + Tailwind, Vite.\n\nLet me check network access for npm/pip.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794318950839,"end":1794318950862}}}
