{"type":"text","timestamp":1794318959864,"sessionID":"ses_e3a41e784ffewW0a3KF7BSFPAW","part":{"id":"prt_1c5be84d000101mPbB7pFU3Nik","messageID":"msg_1c5be72f80019KQ5AN390LweF3","sessionID":"ses_e3a41e784ffewW0a3KF7BSFPAW","type":"text","text":"<think>npm registry works. Now let me check pip. The pip command failed only because of workdir outside workspace? No — the first pip one was blocked because workdir was /tmp/opencode... wait no, the first one was `cd /tmp/opencode && pip download ...`. The blocked one had workdir /tmp/opencode. The second blocked was npm view with workdir /tmp/opencode. Hmm, but the rule says \"/tmp/opencode/*\" is allowed. The issue may be the `cd` command. Let me just test pip from /workspace.\n\nActually, I plan to avoid extra Python dependencies entirely — use stdlib hashlib pbkdf2 + secrets for tokens. That keeps the lock file valid. Let me verify pip works anyway for potential needs.\n\nLet me check the tailwind version to use. Tailwind v4 uses `@tailwindcss/vite` plugin. Let me check versions of @tailwindcss/vite.\n\nAlso vite 8.3.5 — does @tailwindcss/vite support vite 8? Let me check.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794318959824,"end":1794318959858}}}
