{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794319126503,"sessionID":"ses_e3a41e784ffewW0a3KF7BSFPAW","part":{"id":"prt_1c5c10fd5001dVb6q4UjWwH0p6","messageID":"msg_1c5c102ed001U6DkoeSPErJYSX","sessionID":"ses_e3a41e784ffewW0a3KF7BSFPAW","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794319126503,"sessionID":"ses_e3a41e784ffewW0a3KF7BSFPAW","part":{"id":"prt_1c5c10fd80013m2Us53VNw54vT","messageID":"msg_1c5c102ed001U6DkoeSPErJYSX","sessionID":"ses_e3a41e784ffewW0a3KF7BSFPAW","type":"text","text":"<think>Wait: login with missing fields → I return 401 with error \"username is required\". Hmm, should a malformed login be 400 or 401? \"requests that need a signed-in user answer 401 without a valid token\" — that's about protected endpoints. For login with a missing password, 400 is more correct semantically. But a test might check that login with wrong credentials returns 401. Missing fields → I'd say 400. Let me make login return 400 for malformed input (missing username/password), and 401 for wrong credentials. That's the most standard.\n\nLet me restructure: `_credentials` returns an error; in login, return 400 for validation errors, 401 for bad credentials.\n\nHmm, but \"invalid username or password\" with 401 covers both unknown user and wrong password. Good.\n\nLet me update login to use 400 for the validation error.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794319126488,"end":1794319126500}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794319126527,"sessionID":"ses_e3a41e784ffewW0a3KF7BSFPAW","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_01a1c5c10c5e76c3b2cc4c25","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/backend/auth.py","newString":"    credentials, error = _credentials(body)\n    if error:\n        return jsonify({\"error\": error}), 400\n\n    username, password = credentials\n    user = _find_user(username)","oldString":"    credentials, error = _credentials(body)\n    if error:\n        return jsonify({\"error\": error}), 401\n\n    username, password = credentials\n    user = _find_user(username)"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /workspace/backend/auth.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/auth.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/auth.py\n@@ -84,9 +84,9 @@\n     return jsonify({\"error\": error}), 400\n \n credentials, error = _credentials(body)\n if error:\n-    return jsonify({\"error\": error}), 401\n+    return jsonify({\"error\": error}), 400\n \n username, password = credentials\n user = _find_user(username)\n if user is None or not verify_password(password, user[\"password_hash\"]):\n","filediff":{"file":"/workspace/backend/auth.py","patch":"Index: /workspace/backend/auth.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/auth.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/auth.py\n@@ -84,9 +84,9 @@\n     return jsonify({\"error\": error}), 400\n \n credentials, error = _credentials(body)\n if error:\n-    return jsonify({\"error\": error}), 401\n+    return jsonify({\"error\": error}), 400\n \n username, password = credentials\n user = _find_user(username)\n if user is None or not verify_password(password, user[\"password_hash\"]):\n","additions":1,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"backend/auth.py","time":{"start":1794319126496,"end":1794319126510}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[