{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794319298037,"sessionID":"ses_e3a41e784ffewW0a3KF7BSFPAW","part":{"id":"prt_1c5c3adce0019Z3DFhSM2TQpFU","messageID":"msg_1c5c399b1001dpG9ecpR260zwr","sessionID":"ses_e3a41e784ffewW0a3KF7BSFPAW","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794319298038,"sessionID":"ses_e3a41e784ffewW0a3KF7BSFPAW","part":{"id":"prt_1c5c3add5001p4DS8TwIAZ1G0G","messageID":"msg_1c5c399b1001dpG9ecpR260zwr","sessionID":"ses_e3a41e784ffewW0a3KF7BSFPAW","type":"text","text":"<think>There's an HTTP proxy: `HTTP_PROXY=http://llm-gateway:8080` and `NO_PROXY` doesn't include the pip index host, so pip should route through the proxy. But the error said \"cannot reach 172.30.98.3:3141: [Errno 113] No route to host\" — that was from my curl, which... curl uses http_proxy env var too. Hmm, the curl error came from the proxy itself (the gateway couldn't reach the upstream). So the pypi proxy is temporarily unreachable? Let me retry — maybe it's flaky or requires a specific path.\n\nLet me test pip download again and check if the proxy works with a different host (e.g., pypi.org directly through the gateway).\n\nActually the earlier `pip download pyjwt` said \"from versions: none\" — consistent with the proxy returning an error page.\n\nLet me retry a few times.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794319298005,"end":1794319298032}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794319312464,"sessionID":"ses_e3a41e784ffewW0a3KF7BSFPAW","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01a1c5c3a8f374deb6092aac","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"for i in 1 2 3; do timeout 60 curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\\n\" \"http://172.30.98.3:3141/root/pypi/+simple/flask/\"; sleep 2; done; echo \"--- direct pypi via gateway ---\"; timeout 60 curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\\n\" \"https://pypi.org/simple/flask/\"","workdir":"/workspace"},"output":"502\n502\n502\n--- direct pypi via gateway ---\n200\n","metadata":{"output":"502\n502\n502\n--- direct pypi via gateway ---\n200\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"for i in 1 2 3; do timeout 60 curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\\n\" \"http://172.30.98.3:3141/root/pypi/+simple/flask/\"; sleep 2; done; echo \"--- direct pypi via gateway ---\"; timeout 60 curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\\n\" \"https://pypi.org/simple/flask/\"","time":{"start":1794319298021,"end":1794319312446}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c5c3addb001Scbeo1nF9eKJkC","sessionID":"ses_e3a41e784ffewW0a3KF7BSFPAW","messageID":"msg_1c5c399b1001dpG9ecpR260zwr"}}
