{"type":"text","timestamp":1794319465835,"sessionID":"ses_e3a41e784ffewW0a3KF7BSFPAW","part":{"id":"prt_1c5c63d57001tC2dm518IkhPPw","messageID":"msg_1c5c5d1c9001QhnjC1GNotRr78","sessionID":"ses_e3a41e784ffewW0a3KF7BSFPAW","type":"text","text":"<think>Careful: `allowImportingTsExtensions` requires noEmit — ok, we have noEmit true. But vite.config.ts is included and uses `defineConfig` import — with `types: [\"vite/client\"]` that's fine.\n\nHmm, `verbatimModuleSyntax: true` requires type-only imports to use `import type`. I'll be careful in my code.\n\nAlso including vite.config.ts in the same tsconfig with `allowImportingTsExtensions` is fine.\n\nWait, `noUnusedLocals`/`noUnusedParameters` might cause build failures for minor things; I'll make sure the code is clean.\n\nNow the Tailwind entry CSS file and the app.\n\nLet me design the UI carefully.\n\n**Theme**: light, modern, clean. Colors: slate background, white cards, indigo accent. \n\nLayout:\n- `min-h-screen bg-slate-100 text-slate-900`\n- Container: `mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl px-4 py-8`\n\n**Auth screen**: centered card with title \"Todo App\", toggle between \"Sign in\" and \"Create account\", username + password inputs, submit button, error message.\n\n**Board**:\n- Header: app title + username + Sign out button.\n- Stats card: \"N open todos\" counter, plus total count.\n- Controls: tabs (All / Open / Completed) + priority select.\n- Add form: title input, priority select, due date input, description input (optional), Add button. Validation error display.\n- List: rows with checkbox, title, priority badge, due date (highlighted if overdue), edit/delete buttons.\n- Load more button when remaining > 0.\n\nLet me write the files:\n\n1. `src/types.ts`\n2. `src/lib/api.ts`\n3. `src/lib/format.ts` — date helpers + priority styling\n4. `src/components/AuthScreen.tsx`\n5. `src/components/TodoBoard.tsx`\n6. `src/components/TodoRow.tsx`\n7. `src/components/AddTodoForm.tsx`\n8. `src/components/Tabs.tsx` (maybe inline in TodoBoard)\n9. `src/App.tsx`\n10. `src/index.css`\n11. `src/main.tsx`\n\nLet me write the API client.\n\n```ts\nexport type Todo = {\n  id: number;\n  title: string;\n  description: string | null;\n  priority: string;\n  due_date: string | null;\n  completed: boolean;\n  completed_at: string | null;\n  created_at: string;\n};\n\nexport type TodoList = {\n  items: Todo[];\n  total: number;\n  page: number;\n  page_size: number;\n  remaining: number;\n};\n\nexport type TodoInput = {\n  title?: string;\n  description?: string | null;\n  priority?: string;\n  due_date?: string | null;\n  completed?: boolean;\n};\n```\n\napi.ts:\n\n```ts\nconst API_BASE = \"/api\";\n\nexport class ApiError extends Error {\n  readonly status: number;\n  constructor(message: string, status: number) {\n    super(message);\n    this.name = \"ApiError\";\n    this.status = status;\n  }\n}\n\ntype RequestOptions = {\n  method?: string;\n  body?: unknown;\n  token?: string | null;\n};\n\nasync function request<T>(path: string, options: RequestOptions = {}): Promise<T> {\n  const headers: Record<string, string> = { Accept: \"application/json\" };\n  if (options.body !== undefined) headers[\"Content-Type\"] = \"application/json\";\n  if (options.token) headers.Authorization = `Bearer ${options.token}`;\n\n  let response: Response;\n  try {\n    response = await fetch(`${API_BASE}${path}`, {\n      method: options.method ?? \"GET\",\n      headers,\n      body: options.body === undefined ? undefined : JSON.stringify(options.body),\n    });\n  } catch {\n    throw new ApiError(\"Could not reach the server. Please try again.\", 0);\n  }\n\n  const text = await response.text();\n  let payload: unknown = null;\n  if (text) {\n    try { payload = JSON.parse(text); } catch { payload = null; }\n  }\n\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    const message =\n      payload && typeof payload === \"object\" && \"error\" in payload && typeof (payload as {error: unknown}).error === \"string\"\n        ? (payload as {error: string}).error\n        : `Request failed with status ${response.status}`;\n    throw new ApiError(message, response.status);\n  }\n  return payload as T;\n}\n```\n\nThen the api object.\n\nAlso token storage helper in `lib/session.ts`:\n```ts\nconst TOKEN_KEY = \"todo.token\";\nexport function loadToken(): string | null { try { return localStorage.getItem(TOKEN_KEY); } catch { return null; } }\nexport function saveToken(token: string) { try { localStorage.setItem(TOKEN_KEY, token); } catch {} }\nexport function clearToken() { try { localStorage.removeItem(TOKEN_KEY); } catch {} }\n```\n\nNote `catch {}` empty block — with TS, `catch {}` is fine.\n\nformat.ts:\n```ts\nexport function todayIso(): string {\n  const now = new Date();\n  const month = `${now.getMonth() + 1}`.padStart(2, \"0\");\n  const day = `${now.getDate()}`.padStart(2, \"0\");\n  return `${now.getFullYear()}-${month}-${day}`;\n}\n\nexport function isOverdue(todo: Todo): boolean {\n  return !todo.completed && todo.due_date !== null && todo.due_date < todayIso();\n}\n\nexport function formatDueDate(value: string | null): string | null {\n  if (!value) return null;\n  const [y, m, d] = value.split(\"-\");\n  const date = new Date(Number(y), Number(m) - 1, Number(d));\n  if (Number.isNaN(date.getTime())) return value;\n  return date.toLocaleDateString(undefined, { year: \"numeric\", month: \"short\", day: \"numeric\" });\n}\n```\n\nPriority styles:\n```ts\nconst PRIORITY_STYLES: Record<string, string> = {\n  high: \"bg-rose-100 text-rose-700 ring-rose-200\",\n  medium: \"bg-amber-100 text-amber-800 ring-amber-200\",\n  low: \"bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-700 ring-emerald-200\",\n};\nexport function priorityStyle(priority: string): string {\n  return PRIORITY_STYLES[priority.toLowerCase()] ?? \"bg-slate-100 text-slate-700 ring-slate-200\";\n}\nexport function priorityLabel(priority: string): string {\n  return priority.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + priority.slice(1);\n}\n```\n\nPRIORITY_OPTIONS = [\"low\", \"medium\", \"high\"].\n\nNow App.tsx:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useCallback, useEffect, useState } from \"react\";\nimport { AuthScreen } from \"./components/AuthScreen\";\nimport { TodoBoard } from \"./components/TodoBoard\";\nimport { api, ApiError } from \"./lib/api\";\nimport { clearToken, loadToken, saveToken } from \"./lib/session\";\n\nexport default function App() {\n  const [token, setToken] = useState<string | null>(() => loadToken());\n  const [username, setUsername] = useState<string>(\"\");\n  const [checking, setChecking] = useState<boolean>(() => Boolean(loadToken()));\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nOn mount, if a token is stored, fetch /api/auth/me to get the username; if it fails with 401 → clear the token and show the auth screen.\n\nHmm: this requires the token to be validated. If offline → show error. Let me handle: on failure with 401 → clear token; other errors → keep token and let the board try (the board will show the error). Actually simpler: if me() fails with any error, if 401 → sign out; else keep the token and set the username to \"\" and let the board load. The board will show an error if the token is invalid, and on 401 it calls onUnauthorized → sign out.\n\nLet me implement a `signOut` function in App that clears the token and resets state.\n\nTodoBoard handles 401 by calling `onUnauthorized()`.\n\nLet me write TodoBoard:\n\n```tsx\ntype Props = {\n  token: string;\n  username: string;\n  onSignOut: () => void;\n};\n\ntype Tab = \"all\" | \"open\" | \"completed\";\n\nconst PAGE_SIZE = 10;\n\nexport function TodoBoard({ token, username, onSignOut }: Props) {\n  const [tab, setTab] = useState<Tab>(\"all\");\n  const [priority, setPriority] = useState<string>(\"\");\n  const [items, setItems] = useState<Todo[]>([]);\n  const [total, setTotal] = useState(0);\n  const [remaining, setRemaining] = useState(0);\n  const [pages, setPages] = useState(1);\n  const [openCount, setOpenCount] = useState(0);\n  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);\n  const [loadingMore, setLoadingMore] = useState(false);\n  const [error, setError] = useState(\"\");\n  const [reloadToken, setReloadToken] = useState(0);\n```\n\nThe query params depend on tab/priority:\n\n```tsx\nconst query = useMemo(() => {\n  const params: ListParams = { page: 1, page_size: PAGE_SIZE };\n  if (tab === \"open\") params.completed = false;\n  if (tab === \"completed\") params.completed = true;\n  if (priority) params.priority = priority;\n  return params;\n}, [tab, priority]);\n```\n\nload function:\n\n```tsx\nconst fetchPage = useCallback((page: number) => api.listTodos(token, { ...query, page }), [token, query]);\n\nconst load = useCallback(async (pageCount: number) => {\n  setLoading(true);\n  setError(\"\");\n  try {\n    const pagesData = await Promise.all(Array.from({length: pageCount}, (_, i) => fetchPage(i + 1)));\n    const merged = pagesData.flatMap(p => p.items);\n    setItems(merged);\n    setTotal(pagesData[0].total);\n    setRemaining(Math.max(0, pagesData[0].total - merged.length));\n    setPages(pageCount);\n  } catch (err) {\n    handleError(err);\n  } finally {\n    setLoading(false);\n  }\n}, [fetchPage, handleError]);\n```\n\nCareful with `useEffect` dependencies and the `reloadToken` counter to re-run loads after mutations.\n\nI'll use an effect:\n```tsx\nuseEffect(() => {\n  let cancelled = false;\n  ...\n}, [tab, priority, reloadToken]);\n```\nSimplest: an effect that reloads from page 1 whenever tab/priority/reloadToken changes.\n\nAnd a separate effect to fetch the open count whenever reloadToken changes (and on tab change? the open count doesn't depend on the tab).\n\nLet me write it concretely:\n\n```tsx\nuseEffect(() => {\n  let active = true;\n  async function run() {\n    setLoading(true);\n    setError(\"\");\n    try {\n      const [first, open] = await Promise.all([\n        api.listTodos(token, { ...query, page: 1 }),\n        api.listTodos(token, { completed: false, page: 1, page_size: 1 }),\n      ]);\n      if (!active) return;\n      setItems(first.items);\n      setTotal(first.total);\n      setRemaining(first.remaining);\n      setPages(1);\n      setOpenCount(open.total);\n    } catch (err) {\n      if (!active) return;\n      handleError(err);\n    } finally {\n      if (active) setLoading(false);\n    }\n  }\n  run();\n  return () => { active = false; };\n}, [token, query, reloadToken, handleError]);\n```\n\nNote: `query` changes identity when tab/priority change → the effect re-runs. Good. But `handleError` must be stable (useCallback with token dep).\n\nBut careful: after a mutation (e.g. toggling a checkbox) I want the list refreshed with the current page count preserved (e.g. if the user loaded 3 pages, after a toggle we should reload 3 pages). Let me handle mutations with a dedicated function that reloads `pages` pages:\n\n```tsx\nconst refresh = useCallback(async (pageCount = pages) => { ... }, [...]);\n```\n\nLet me restructure: keep a `reload(pageCount)` function that fetches pageCount pages and merges; the effect calls reload(1); mutations call reload(pages).\n\nI'll implement:\n\n```tsx\nconst reload = useCallback(async (pageCount: number) => {\n  setLoading(true);\n  setError(\"\");\n  try {\n    const results = await Promise.all(\n      Array.from({ length: pageCount }, (_, index) => api.listTodos(token, { ...query, page: index + 1 })),\n    );\n    const merged = results.flatMap((result) => result.items);\n    setItems(merged);\n    setTotal(results[0].total);\n    setRemaining(Math.max(0, results[0].total - merged.length));\n    setPages(pageCount);\n  } catch (err) {\n    handleError(err);\n  } finally {\n    setLoading(false);\n  }\n}, [token, query, handleError]);\n```\n\nAnd the open count effect separately:\n```tsx\nuseEffect(() => {\n  let active = true;\n  api.listTodos(token, { completed: false, page: 1, page_size: 1 })\n    .then((result) => { if (active) setOpenCount(result.total); })\n    .catch(() => {});\n  return () => { active = false; };\n}, [token, reloadToken]);\n```\n\nHmm, but `reload` in the effect depends on `query`, so it re-runs when the tab changes. The effect:\n```tsx\nuseEffect(() => { void reload(1); }, [reload]);\n```\n`reload` identity changes when query changes → good.\n\nWait, there's an issue: `reload` also depends on `handleError` and `token`. Fine.\n\nBut the effect will re-run whenever `reload` changes identity — which happens when query changes. Good.\n\nMutations: after create/update/delete → `void reload(pages)` plus `setReloadToken(t => t+1)` to refresh the open count. Hmm, but setReloadToken would also re-trigger the `reload(1)` effect if reload depends on reloadToken — it doesn't. Good, the open-count effect depends on reloadToken.\n\nLet me make sure the open count effect and the reload effect don't conflict. They run independently. Good.\n\nLoad more:\n```tsx\nconst loadMore = async () => {\n  setLoadingMore(true);\n  setError(\"\");\n  try {\n    const result = await api.listTodos(token, { ...query, page: pages + 1 });\n    setItems(prev => [...prev, ...result.items]);\n    setTotal(result.total);\n    setRemaining(result.remaining);\n    setPages(pages + 1);\n  } catch (err) { handleError(err); }\n  finally { setLoadingMore(false); }\n};\n```\n\nToggle:\n```tsx\nconst toggle = async (todo: Todo) => {\n  try {\n    const updated = await api.updateTodo(token, todo.id, { completed: !todo.completed });\n    setItems(prev => prev.map(item => item.id === updated.id ? updated : item));\n    setReloadToken(t => t + 1);  // refresh open count\n  } catch (err) { setError(message(err)); }\n};\n```\nBut if the updated todo no longer matches the current tab filter (e.g. the \"open\" tab), it should be removed from the list. Let me apply the filter client-side after the update:\n\n```tsx\nsetItems(prev => prev.map(item => item.id === updated.id ? updated : item).filter(item => matchesFilter(item, tab, priority)));\n```\nwhere matchesFilter checks completed state and priority.\n\nThat keeps the list consistent without a full reload. But the total counts would be stale; a reload is cleaner. Let me just do `await reload(pages)` after mutations — simple and always correct. The downside: a full re-fetch of all loaded pages on each toggle. With page_size 10 and a few pages, negligible.\n\nI'll do: optimistic local update + `reload(pages)` to sync. Actually, simplest and most predictable: after a mutation, call `reload(pages)`. Let me do that (no optimistic update) — the UI will just refresh. For the checkbox \"saves immediately\", a brief delay is OK.\n\nHmm, but there's a subtlety: if the user toggles a checkbox in the \"open\" tab, the todo disappears from the list after the reload. That's correct behavior.\n\nCreate:\n```tsx\nconst create = async (input: TodoInput) => {\n  const created = await api.createTodo(token, input);\n  await reload(1)?  // or reload(pages)\n  setReloadToken(t => t + 1);\n};\n```\nAfter creating, if the current filter doesn't match the new todo, it won't show. I'll reload the current pages; the new todo appears if it matches the filter. Good.\n\nUpdate (inline edit): after a successful PATCH, update the item in place and reload to sync ordering (the due date may have changed → order changes). So reload(pages).\n\nDelete: after DELETE → reload(pages) and update the open count.\n\nError handling for 401 → onSignOut().\n\nLet me write `handleError`:\n```tsx\nconst handleError = useCallback((err: unknown) => {\n  if (err instanceof ApiError) {\n    if (err.status === 401) { onUnauthorized(); return; }\n    setError(err.message);\n    return;\n  }\n  setError(\"Something went wrong. Please try again.\");\n}, [onUnauthorized]);\n```\n\nNow the components.\n\n**TodoRow** props:\n```tsx\ntype Props = {\n  todo: Todo;\n  onToggle: (todo: Todo) => Promise<void> | void;\n  onUpdate: (id: number, patch: TodoInput) => Promise<string | null>;  // returns error message or null\n  onDelete: (todo: Todo) => Promise<void> | void;\n  busy?: boolean;\n};\n```\n\nHmm, for inline editing errors, the row needs the error message from the API. Let me have `onUpdate` return a promise that rejects with the ApiError, and the row catches it and displays `err.message`. That's clean:\n\n```tsx\nconst save = async () => {\n  setSaving(true);\n  setError(\"\");\n  try {\n    await onUpdate(todo.id, { title, description, priority, due_date });\n    setEditing(false);\n  } catch (err) {\n    setError(err instanceof ApiError ? err.message : \"Could not save the changes.\");\n  } finally {\n    setSaving(false);\n  }\n};\n```\n\nAnd the parent `onUpdate` should NOT swallow errors → it should rethrow. Let me define the parent's update handler to throw on error so the row can display the message. The parent also sets a global error? Better not to duplicate. I'll have the parent rethrow and let the row display it.\n\nFor the add form, the AddTodoForm component handles its own error display similarly.\n\nLet me now write the row UI:\n\n```tsx\n<li className=\"rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 shadow-sm\">\n  <div className=\"flex items-start gap-3\">\n    <input type=\"checkbox\" checked={todo.completed} onChange={() => onToggle(todo)} className=\"mt-1 h-5 w-5 rounded border-slate-300 text-indigo-600 focus:ring-indigo-500\" />\n    <div className=\"min-w-0 flex-1\">\n      <div className=\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2\">\n        <span className={title classes}>{todo.title}</span>\n        <span className={badge classes}>{priorityLabel(todo.priority)}</span>\n        {dueDate && <span className={due classes}>{overdue ? \"Overdue · \" : \"\"}{formatDueDate(dueDate)}</span>}\n      </div>\n      {todo.description && <p className=\"mt-1 text-sm text-slate-500\">{todo.description}</p>}\n    </div>\n    <div className=\"flex items-center gap-2\">\n      <button onClick={() => setEditing(!editing)}>Edit</button>\n      <button onClick={() => setConfirming(true)}>Delete</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  {confirming && <div>Delete this todo? <button>Delete</button><button>Cancel</button></div>}\n  {editing && <form>...</form>}\n  {error && <p className=\"text-rose-600\">{error}</p>}\n</li>\n```\n\nOverdue highlight: the due date text in red + the row gets a red-tinted left border or background: `border-rose-300 bg-rose-50/40`.\n\nNow the inline edit form fields: title (input), description (textarea), priority (select), due date (input type=date), Save/Cancel buttons, and the error message.\n\nNote: `due_date` from the API is \"YYYY-MM-DD\" → the date input value works directly.\n\n**AddTodoForm**: title input (required), priority select, due date input, description input, Add button. On submit → call onCreate; if it throws, show the error message.\n\nLet me write the code. I'll use a shared `fieldClasses` constant for inputs.\n\nAlso, the \"counter of open todos\": show \"N open\" in the header/summary card.\n\nTabs: All / Open / Completed buttons with active styling.\n\nPriority filter: a `<select>` with All priorities / Low / Medium / High.\n\nLoad more button: shown when remaining > 0; label \"Load more (N remaining)\".\n\nLet me write all the files now.\n\nOne more consideration for `App.tsx`: the AuthScreen needs to handle both login and register. Let me write it with a mode toggle.\n\nAuthScreen props: `{ onSignedIn: (token: string, username: string) => void }`.\n\n```tsx\nexport function AuthScreen({ onSignedIn }: Props) {\n  const [mode, setMode] = useState<\"login\" | \"register\">(\"login\");\n  const [username, setUsername] = useState(\"\");\n  const [password, setPassword] = useState(\"\");\n  const [error, setError] = useState(\"\");\n  const [busy, setBusy] = useState(false);\n\n  const submit = async (event: FormEvent) => {\n    event.preventDefault();\n    setBusy(true); setError(\"\");\n    try {\n      if (mode === \"register\") {\n        const result = await api.register(username, password);\n        saveToken(result.token);\n        onSignedIn(result.token, result.username);\n      } else {\n        const result = await api.login(username, password);\n        saveToken(result.token);\n        onSignedIn(result.token, username.trim());\n      }\n    } catch (err) {\n      setError(err instanceof ApiError ? err.message : \"...\");\n    } finally { setBusy(false); }\n  };\n```\n\nThe register response includes \"username\" and \"token\". Good.\n\nNow let me write everything.\n\nFor the tab buttons, an accessible implementation: use buttons with aria-pressed.\n\nLet me write the files.</think>\n\nNow the frontend source files:","time":{"start":1794319465815,"end":1794319465829}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794319465860,"sessionID":"ses_e3a41e784ffewW0a3KF7BSFPAW","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_01a1c5c6396070d18c9a2903","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"export type Todo = {\n  id: number;\n  title: string;\n  description: string | null;\n  priority: string;\n  due_date: string | null;\n  completed: boolean;\n  completed_at: string | null;\n  created_at: string;\n};\n\nexport type TodoPage = {\n  items: Todo[];\n  total: number;\n  page: number;\n  page_size: number;\n  remaining: number;\n};\n\nexport type TodoInput = {\n  title?: string;\n  description?: string | null;\n  priority?: string;\n  due_date?: string | null;\n  completed?: boolean;\n};\n\nexport type ListParams = {\n  completed?: boolean;\n  priority?: string;\n  page?: number;\n  page_size?: number;\n};\n","filePath":"/workspace/frontend/src/types.ts"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/workspace/frontend/src/types.ts","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"frontend/src/types.ts","time":{"start":1794319465825,"end":1794319465838}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c5c63d5a001lYfWStdfZidBxj","sessionID":"ses_e3a41e784ffewW0a3KF7BSFPAW","messageID":"msg_1c5c5d1c9001QhnjC1GNotRr78"}}
