{"type":"text","timestamp":1794319599940,"sessionID":"ses_e3a41e784ffewW0a3KF7BSFPAW","part":{"id":"prt_1c5c84931001smEe8zYIxGqnHo","messageID":"msg_1c5c830b8001Z5JY7tqBJNC24v","sessionID":"ses_e3a41e784ffewW0a3KF7BSFPAW","type":"text","text":"<think>No browser available. Installing playwright + chromium would be a large download; the npm registry works though. It could be valuable to verify the UI works (React rendering, no runtime errors). Let me consider: `npx playwright install chromium` downloads ~150MB. It might work through the proxy. It's worth trying since a broken UI would be a major failure. But it's a \"nice to have\" — the code is straightforward React.\n\nAlternative lighter check: use jsdom to render the App with a mocked fetch? That requires installing jsdom + a test runner. Also heavy-ish but much lighter than chromium.\n\nLet me try playwright — it gives a real browser check of the whole app. First check if the download works.\n\nActually, let me first finish the remaining work (backend tests, docs), then try the browser check if time permits.\n\nLet me try installing playwright quickly in the background while I continue.\n\nActually, let's just try it — npm i -D playwright in a temp dir (not the frontend, to avoid polluting package.json/lock). I'll install into /workspace/.e2e (gitignored?). Hmm, adding files to the workspace could pollute the repo. I'll create /workspace/.e2e and delete it afterwards. But .dockerignore doesn't exclude it... I'll delete it when done.\n\nLet me check .gitignore — there's no .gitignore in the workspace! The .dockerignore excludes node_modules etc. but the data dir and .venv aren't excluded... wait: .dockerignore has `**/node_modules`, `**/.venv`, `data/*.db`. OK.\n\nLet me try the playwright install in a temp dir under /workspace (since /tmp/opencode seems to have permission issues with writes? Earlier the redirect to /tmp/opencode/gunicorn.log failed with permission denied. So /tmp/opencode isn't writable. I'll use /workspace/.tmp-e2e and remove it later.\n\nLet me kick that off in the background.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794319599921,"end":1794319599936}}}
